{"step_index":566,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:12:38Z","content":"To use **`th2-dnsp-mst1`** (`172.30.198.162:8081`, the authoritative PowerDNS master for `outremer-telecom.fr`), here is what we need to adjust before the playbook can run successfully:\n\n---\n\n### What Needs to Be Updated in [`~/.ansible/`](file:///home/koby/.ansible)\n\n1. **PowerDNS Hook Zone Fix**:\n   In [`~/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh), line 17 currently assumes:\n   ```bash\n   zone=\"${CERTBOT_DOMAIN}.\"\n   ```\n   For `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, PowerDNS does not have a dedicated sub-zone; the zone on `th2-dnsp-mst1` is **`outremer-telecom.fr.`**. We need to make the hook write to `outremer-telecom.fr.`.\n\n2. **PowerDNS API Key in Vault**:\n   In [`~/.ansible/playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml), the PowerDNS section currently has placeholder values:\n   ```yaml\n   vault_powerdns_api_url: \"https://dnsp-mst.example.lan/api/v1\"\n   vault_powerdns_api_key: \"CLE_API_POWERDNS_ICI\"\n   vault_powerdns_dns_host: \"dnsp-mst.example.lan\"\n   ```\n   To point to `th2-dnsp-mst1`, it must be:\n   ```yaml\n   vault_powerdns_api_url: \"http://172.30.198.162:8081\"\n   vault_powerdns_dns_host: \"172.30.198.162\"\n   vault_powerdns_api_key: \"<REAL_API_KEY>\"\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Two Options to Proceed\n\n#### Option 1: Run via the Local Playbook (`~/.ansible/playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml`)\n* I will fix the zone extraction in [`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh).\n* You provide the `th2-dnsp-mst1` API key (or update [`group_vars/all/vault.yml`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml) with `ansible-vault edit`).\n* We run `ansible-playbook playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml` right from your terminal.\n\n#### Option 2: Use Semaphore Template 53 (`infra-management-system`)\n* In [`infra-management-system/playbooks/issue-le-cert.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/playbooks/issue-le-cert.yml), `th2-dnsp-mst1` and `outremer-telecom.fr` are already natively integrated (the same way `drive.outremer-telecom.fr`, `onetask`, and `postfix` were issued).\n* The PowerDNS API key is already stored and attached in Semaphore Key Store (Vault ID 2).\n* We just add `map_extranetclient` to `le_targets_map` in `issue-le-cert.yml`, commit to `main`, and run Template **53 (`Issue LE cert (public) - PROD`)** in Semaphore.\n\nWhich option do you prefer?","thinking":"**Evaluating Playbook Execution Requirements**\n\nThe initial request involves running a playbook for certificate issuance. A previous check confirmed the playbook's existence. The subsequent instruction specifies `th2-dnsp-mst1` for the DNS challenge. The objective is to determine how to incorporate this DNS challenge information when executing the playbook.\n\n\n**Identifying Playbook Dependencies**\n\nExamining the playbook's configuration reveals dependencies on PowerDNS for DNS challenges and several relevant variables. The current PowerDNS API key is a placeholder, which will result in an unauthorized error during hook execution. Also, the defined DNS zone does not match the expected zone format used in the certbot hook.\n\n\n**Assessing Playbook Run Readiness**\n\nThe production playbook uses the correct server and zone name format. The placeholder API key and incorrect zone configuration still present are the blockers. The certificate deployment playbook requires a valid API key and a zone name that aligns with the DNS hook's expectations. Two possible routes to address this are updating variables and the hook directly, or using the pre-configured production playbook.\n\n\n"}
