{"step_index":568,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:13:59Z","thinking":"**Identifying PowerDNS API Key Dependency**\n\nThe first requirement involves obtaining the correct API key for the PowerDNS instance located at a specific address, accessed via port 8081. This API key is essential for authentication, and is referenced using a specific HTTP header. The key's location is either within a configuration file on the specified host, or potentially within a secure vault. The user might need to provide this key.\n\n\n**Preparing for certificate issuance**\n\nThe PowerDNS API key can be set directly or within a secure vault file. Hook scripts require adaptation to either accept or derive the authoritative DNS zone, ensuring flexibility for various domain configurations.\n\nA new entry must be added to a configuration file to declare the target host and certificate details.  Connectivity to the target host through SSH must be confirmed for deployment; issuing certificates separately is an alternative approach if needed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh","toolAction":"Viewing pdns-cleanup-hook.sh","toolSummary":"View pdns-cleanup-hook.sh"}}]}
{"step_index":569,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:14:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T17:14:05+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T17:14:05+04:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`\nTotal Lines: 21\nTotal Bytes: 828\nShowing lines 1 to 21\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env bash\n2: # Hook de nettoyage DNS-01 pour certbot --manual — backend PowerDNS (dnsp-mst).\n3: # Appelé par certbot après la validation (succès ou échec) pour retirer le TXT.\n4: set -euo pipefail\n5: \n6: : \"${PDNS_API_URL:?PDNS_API_URL non défini}\"\n7: : \"${PDNS_API_KEY:?PDNS_API_KEY non défini}\"\n8: : \"${CERTBOT_DOMAIN:?CERTBOT_DOMAIN non défini}\"\n9: \n10: record_name=\"_acme-challenge.${CERTBOT_DOMAIN}.\"\n11: zone=\"${CERTBOT_DOMAIN}.\"\n12: \n13: # Ne doit jamais faire échouer le nettoyage : certbot doit pouvoir terminer\n14: # proprement même si le enregistrement est déjà absent.\n15: curl -sf -X PATCH \\\n16:   -H \"X-API-Key: ${PDNS_API_KEY}\" \\\n17:   -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n18:   \"${PDNS_API_URL}/servers/localhost/zones/${zone}\" \\\n19:   -d \"{\\\"rrsets\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"${record_name}\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"TXT\\\",\\\"changetype\\\":\\\"DELETE\\\"}]}\" \\\n20:   >/dev/null || true\n21: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":570,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:14:05Z","content":"For **Option 1**, here is everything that is needed:\n\n### 1. From you (Only 1 item needed)\n\n* **The PowerDNS API Key** for `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`http://172.30.198.162:8081`).\n  * *Where to find it*: In `/etc/powerdns/pdns.conf` (directive `api-key=...`) on `th2-dnsp-mst1`, or in the Semaphore Key Store (Vault ID 2).\n  * You can either share it here so I insert it, or edit it yourself with:\n    ```bash\n    cd ~/.ansible\n    ansible-vault edit playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml\n    ```\n    and set `vault_powerdns_api_key: \"<YOUR_KEY>\"`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. What I will configure automatically\n\n1. **Fix the PowerDNS Hooks**:\n   * Update [`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh) and [`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh) so they write the challenge to the parent zone **`outremer-telecom.fr.`** rather than trying to look up a non-existent sub-zone `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.`.\n2. **Configure Vault URLs**:\n   * Set `vault_powerdns_api_url: \"http://172.30.198.162:8081\"` and `vault_powerdns_dns_host: \"172.30.198.162\"` in [`playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml).\n3. **Add Domain to Catalogue**:\n   * Add `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to [`playbooks/group_vars/all/certificates.yml`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/group_vars/all/certificates.yml) pointing to `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`).\n4. **Execute the Playbook**:\n   * Run a dry test against Let's Encrypt **staging** (`letsencrypt_staging: true`) to confirm the DNS TXT propagation works cleanly without risking rate limits.\n   * Run production (`letsencrypt_staging: false`) to issue the final certificate and deploy.","thinking":"**Refactoring Domain Zone Handling**\n\nIdentified that domain zone handling in both scripts relies on `CERTBOT_DOMAIN`. This is inflexible. Proposing a `PDNS_ZONE` variable for improved flexibility.\n\nInitial plan is to modify the `zone` variable assignment to use `PDNS_ZONE` with a default, ensuring robustness with a final cleanup step. This will make the process bulletproof.\n\n\n"}
